  "prose": [
    {
      "title": "Allow step select",
      "text": "To disable step selection, set `allowStepSelect` prop on `Stepper.Step` component.\nIt can be used to prevent the user from reaching next steps while letting them go back and forth between steps they've already reached before:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Disable next steps selection",
      "text": "Another way to disable selection of upcoming steps is to use the `allowNextStepsSelect` directly on the `Stepper` component.\nThis is useful when you don't need to control the behavior specifically for each step.",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Color, radius and size",
      "text": "Component size is controlled by two props: `size` and `iconSize`.\n`size` prop controls icon size, label and description font size.\n`iconSize` allows to overwrite icon size separately from other size values:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "With custom icons",
      "text": "You can replace the step icon by setting `icon` prop on `Stepper.Step` component.\nTo change completed check icon set `completedIcon` on `Stepper` component.\nYou can use any React node as an icon: component, string, number:\n\nYou can use `Stepper` with icons only. Note that in this case, you will have to\nset `aria-label` or `title` on `Stepper.Step` component to make it accessible:\n\nYou can also change the completed icon for each step, for example, to indicate error state:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Icon position",
      "text": "To change step icon and body arrangement, set `iconPosition=\"right\"`:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Loading state",
      "text": "To indicate loading state set `loading` prop on Step component, `Loader` will replace step icon.\nYou can configure the default loader in the [theme](/theming/theme-object/).\n\nExamples of styles customization with Styles API:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Get step ref",
      "text": "You can get refs of step button and stepper root element (div):",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Wrap Stepper.Step",
      "text": "`Stepper` component relies on `Stepper.Step` order. Wrapping `Stepper.Step` is not supported,\nInstead you will need to use different approaches:",
      "format": "md"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accessibility",
      "text": "`<Stepper.Step />` components render button element, set `aria-label` or `title` props\nto make component visible for screen readers in case you do not specify `label` or `description`:",
      "format": "md"
    }
  ],
